> d5(b: u5, d: i3) = u5(i16(b) + i16(d))
> dc5(b: u5, d: i3) = u5(min(31, max(0, i16(b) + i16(d))))
> equiv d5 dc5
d5 and dc5 differ at 16 points, e.g. b=0, d=-4: 28 vs 0
> wrap d5
wrap analysis of d5:
  i16(b) + i16(d)   (i16)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 118 points, e.g. b=4, d=-4
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  u5(i16(b) + i16(d))   (u5)
      truncates at 16 points, e.g. b=0, d=-4
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 16 points, e.g. b=0, d=-4
  over all 256 points of the domain
